{"id":"T1110","name":"Brute Force","tactics":["credential-access"],"description":"Adversaries may use brute force techniques to gain access to accounts when passwords are unknown or when password hashes are obtained. Without knowledge of the password for an account or set of accounts, an adversary may systematically guess the password using a repetitive or iterative mechanism. Brute forcing passwords can take place via interaction with a service that will check the validity of those credentials or offline against previously acquired credential data, such as password hashes. Brute forcing credentials may take place at various points during a breach. For example, adversaries ","status":"defended","claimed_by":[{"id":"CIS-4.1","title":""},{"id":"CIS-4.10","title":""},{"id":"CIS-4.7","title":""},{"id":"CIS-5.2","title":""},{"id":"CIS-5.3","title":""},{"id":"CIS-6.3","title":""},{"id":"CIS-6.4","title":""},{"id":"CIS-6.5","title":""}],"live_rules":[{"id":"259a9cdf-c4dd-4fa2-b243-2269e5ab18a2","title":"External Remote RDP Logon from Public IP","level":"medium","requires":["windows/security"]},{"id":"28ecba0a-c743-4690-ad29-9a8f6f25a6f9","title":"Password Spray Activity","level":"high","requires":["azure/riskdetection"]},{"id":"2b7d6fc0-71ac-4cf7-8ed1-b5788ee5257a","title":"Account Lockout","level":"medium","requires":["azure/signinlogs"]},{"id":"53bb4f7f-48a8-4475-ac30-5a82ddfdf6fc","title":"Potential MFA Bypass Using Legacy Client Authentication","level":"high","requires":["azure/signinlogs"]},{"id":"5496ff55-42ec-4369-81cb-00f417029e25","title":"Multifactor Authentication Interrupted","level":"medium","requires":["azure/signinlogs"]},{"id":"60f6535a-760f-42a9-be3f-c9a0a025906e","title":"Use of Legacy Authentication Protocols","level":"high","requires":["azure/signinlogs"]},{"id":"78d5cab4-557e-454f-9fb9-a222bd0d5edc","title":"External Remote SMB Logon from Public IP","level":"high","requires":["windows/security"]},{"id":"8c944ecb-6970-4541-8496-be554b8e2846","title":"Su